# serial_cycle_moved -- the succession with one region moved, which is the
# one thing a re-declaration may never do while a lap is in flight.
#
# Every line here matches `serial_cycle_succession.bron` except one: the
# arc `beech` writes and `cedar` reads is named `ask_bd` rather than
# `ask_bc`. The shape survives the rename whole -- three domains, three
# channels, every region one writer and one reader, one lap closing alder
# to beech to cedar and home -- so a reader that only asks about shape
# reports a ring and hands this document on.
#
# The move is invisible to shape and fatal to the work. A region's backing
# store is addressed by the region's own name, so the asks a running domain
# is placing into `ask_bc` at this very moment land in a store that nobody
# under this document ever reads, and `ask_bd` opens empty at zero. A
# supervisor swapping documents cannot know whether the domain it is
# replacing has already exited or is still writing -- the outcome is
# unreaped by definition -- so a document that is safe under one reading
# and ruinous under the other must be refused under both.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; refused mid-flight by
# `caravan/inflight.rye`.

system serial_cycle_moved

domain alder
domain beech
domain cedar

channel alder beech
channel beech cedar
channel cedar alder

region ask_ab 4096
region ask_bd 4096
region ask_ca 4096
region taken 64

grant ask_ab alder rw
grant ask_ab beech r
grant ask_bd beech rw
grant ask_bd cedar r
grant ask_ca cedar rw
grant ask_ca alder r
grant taken alder rw
grant taken cedar r
